1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
Then it moves on to the relationship with the self.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,680
And when we speak about the relationship with the self,

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:13,080
we say the following: it is built upon

4
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:16,200
a basis?

5
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:18,920
Not on entertainment.

6
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:22,720
Nor on self-esteem, nor on development, nor on

7
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,720
glorification.

8
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:27,800
No — it is built on purification. And Muslim scholars

9
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,720
concerned with behaviour

10
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:37,640
hold that the first gate of purification is that a person thinks ill

11
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:41,160
of himself,

12
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,960
that a person thinks ill of himself,

13
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,680
and thinks well of his Lord and of others.

14
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:52,920
If he thinks well of himself, he grows arrogant, tyrannical and conceited,

15
00:00:53,040 --> 00:01:00,160
is struck by self-admiration, settles for passive contentment, and will not improve it.
